Error [jet.InvalidStatement]: A unit-fallible error contract comes before the effect arrow
  --> tests/ui/unit_fallible_contract_precedes_effect_arrow.jet:11:26
    |
 11 | later: fn(n: Int) -[IO]> MakeError! {
    |                          ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A function that can fail but returns no value has no result after its effect arrow; its error contract is written first
 Fix: Write `MakeError! -[IO]>`, as in `save: fn(path: String) IOError! -[FS]>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0003
